within AnomalyLibrary.UsersGuide;
class Limitations "Modelling assumptions and numerical limits"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Information;
  annotation(Documentation(info="<html><p>The components implement declared deterministic perturbations. Signal and frame operations do not model detailed electronics or a complete communication protocol. Some prescribed physical sources exchange energy with an implicit external environment; their class documentation identifies the relevant power, energy or flow quantities.</p><p>Frame queues and stored command schedules are finite. Select capacities and service periods for the intended workload and inspect overflow, dropped-frame and sequence-error flags. A frame count jump cannot reconstruct missing payloads. Direct physical connection to ideal boundaries must remain a well-posed Modelica model.</p><p>Discontinuities, switching and contact can introduce events or stiff dynamics. Check the numerical behaviour in the selected Modelica environment and compare example outputs with the stated analytical expectations before interpreting a larger model.</p></html>"));
end Limitations;
